Relevant columns and potential usage  

• PUBLICATIONS."publication_number": unique ID of every patent publication – needed for both citing and cited patents.  
• PUBLICATIONS."citation": VARIANT array that lists the patents each publication cites – flatten to obtain the cited "publication_number".  
• PUBLICATIONS."assignee_harmonized": VARIANT array of assignee names – flatten to (i) collect patents assigned to “DENSO CORP” (cited set) and (ii) collect the assignees of the citing patents, later excluding “DENSO CORP”.  
• PUBLICATIONS."filing_date": integer YYYYMMDD – keep only rows where it is not NULL/0 to satisfy “valid filing dates”.  
• PUBLICATIONS."cpc": VARIANT array of CPC codes – flatten and keep the first element (index = 0) to obtain the “primary CPC code” of each citing patent.  
• CPC_DEFINITION."symbol": CPC subclass / subgroup symbol – join to the first 4–7 characters of the primary CPC code.  
• CPC_DEFINITION."titleFull": full written title of that CPC symbol – provides the requested CPC subclass title.  

Typical conditions  

• Valid filing date:  WHERE p."filing_date" IS NOT NULL AND p."filing_date" <> 0  
• Assignee filter (DENSO patents being cited):  assignee.value ILIKE '%DENSO%CORP%'  
• Citing‑side assignee exclusion:  c_assignee.value NOT ILIKE '%DENSO%CORP%'  
• First CPC code only:  WHERE cp.index = 0  
• Join CPC definition on SUBSTR(cp.value:"code"::STRING,1,4) = cd."symbol" (or longer if needed).  

Below are ten incremental Snowflake SQL queries (LIMIT 20 each) that explore the data from simple inspection all the way to the final aggregation.  
(Be sure your role/warehouse has access to the PATENTS database.)

```sql
-- 1. Description: Peek at a few publications that have DENSO CORP as (one of) their assignees.
SELECT DISTINCT 
       p."publication_number",
       a.value::STRING AS "assignee_name"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."assignee_harmonized") a
WHERE a.value::STRING ILIKE '%DENSO%CORP%'
  AND p."filing_date" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Inspect the structure of the "citation" field (one publication flattened).
SELECT 
       p."publication_number"      AS "citing_pub",
       c.value                     AS "raw_citation_json"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."citation") c
WHERE p."publication_number" = 'US-7650331-B1'   -- ← replace with any known pub
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: List DENSO‑assigned publication numbers (distinct).
SELECT DISTINCT
       p."publication_number"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."assignee_harmonized") a
WHERE a.value::STRING ILIKE '%DENSO%CORP%'
  AND p."filing_date" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Show citing/cited pairs (no filtering yet) to verify we can extract the cited publication number.
SELECT 
       p."publication_number"                              AS "citing_pub",
       c.value:"publication_number"::STRING                AS "cited_pub"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."citation") c
WHERE p."filing_date" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Check whether any cited publication belongs to DENSO CORP.
SELECT 
       DISTINCT c.value:"publication_number"::STRING AS "cited_pub"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."citation") c
WHERE c.value:"publication_number"::STRING IS NOT NULL
  AND EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS d,
             LATERAL FLATTEN(input => d."assignee_harmonized") da
        WHERE d."publication_number" = c.value:"publication_number"::STRING
          AND da.value::STRING ILIKE '%DENSO%CORP%'
          AND d."filing_date" IS NOT NULL
      )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Examine the first (primary) CPC code of a random publication to see the value format.
SELECT 
       p."publication_number",
       cp.value:"code"::STRING        AS "primary_cpc_code"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc") cp
WHERE cp.index = 0
  AND p."filing_date" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Map a few CPC codes (first 4 chars) to their full titles from CPC_DEFINITION.
SELECT 
       SUBSTR(cp.value:"code"::STRING,1,4)         AS "ipc4",
       cd."titleFull"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc") cp
JOIN PATENTS.PATENTS.CPC_DEFINITION cd
  ON cd."symbol" = SUBSTR(cp.value:"code"::STRING,1,4)
WHERE cp.index = 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Pull citing publications that cite at least one DENSO patent and get their non‑DENSO assignee plus primary CPC code.
SELECT DISTINCT
       p."publication_number"                           AS "citing_pub",
       ca.value::STRING                                 AS "citing_assignee",
       SUBSTR(cp.value:"code"::STRING,1,7)              AS "primary_cpc",
       cd."titleFull"                                   AS "cpc_title"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p
     -- citing side assignees
     , LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."assignee_harmonized") ca
     -- citing side citations
     , LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."citation") cit
     -- citing side primary CPC
     , LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc") cp
JOIN PATENTS.PATENTS.CPC_DEFINITION cd
  ON cd."symbol" = SUBSTR(cp.value:"code"::STRING,1,4)
WHERE cp.index = 0
  AND cit.value:"publication_number"::STRING IS NOT NULL
  AND p."filing_date" IS NOT NULL
  -- requirement: it cites a DENSO patent
  AND EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS d,
             LATERAL FLATTEN(input => d."assignee_harmonized") da
        WHERE d."publication_number" = cit.value:"publication_number"::STRING
          AND da.value::STRING ILIKE '%DENSO%CORP%'
          AND d."filing_date" IS NOT NULL
      )
  -- exclude DENSO as citing assignee
  AND ca.value::STRING NOT ILIKE '%DENSO%CORP%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Aggregate counts of how many DENSO‑citing links each non‑DENSO assignee has, broken down by CPC subclass title.
SELECT 
       ca.value::STRING                               AS "citing_assignee",
       cd."titleFull"                                 AS "cpc_title",
       COUNT(DISTINCT p."publication_number")         AS "num_citations"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p
     , LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."assignee_harmonized") ca
     , LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."citation") cit
     , LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc") cp
JOIN PATENTS.PATENTS.CPC_DEFINITION cd
  ON cd."symbol" = SUBSTR(cp.value:"code"::STRING,1,4)
WHERE cp.index = 0
  AND p."filing_date" IS NOT NULL
  AND cit.value:"publication_number"::STRING IS NOT NULL
  AND EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS d,
             LATERAL FLATTEN(input => d."assignee_harmonized") da
        WHERE d."publication_number" = cit.value:"publication_number"::STRING
          AND da.value::STRING ILIKE '%DENSO%CORP%'
          AND d."filing_date" IS NOT NULL
      )
  AND ca.value::STRING NOT ILIKE '%DENSO%CORP%'
GROUP BY ca.value::STRING, cd."titleFull"
ORDER BY "num_citations" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: (Final-style) Same as #9 but returns the full list without LIMIT for later export.
SELECT 
       ca.value::STRING                               AS "citing_assignee",
       cd."titleFull"                                 AS "cpc_title",
       COUNT(DISTINCT p."publication_number")         AS "num_citations"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p
     , LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."assignee_harmonized") ca
     , LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."citation") cit
     , LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."cpc") cp
JOIN PATENTS.PATENTS.CPC_DEFINITION cd
  ON cd."symbol" = SUBSTR(cp.value:"code"::STRING,1,4)
WHERE cp.index = 0
  AND p."filing_date" IS NOT NULL
  AND cit.value:"publication_number"::STRING IS NOT NULL
  AND EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS d,
             LATERAL FLATTEN(input => d."assignee_harmonized") da
        WHERE d."publication_number" = cit.value:"publication_number"::STRING
          AND da.value::STRING ILIKE '%DENSO%CORP%'
          AND d."filing_date" IS NOT NULL
      )
  AND ca.value::STRING NOT ILIKE '%DENSO%CORP%'
GROUP BY ca.value::STRING, cd."titleFull"
ORDER BY "num_citations" DESC;
```

